<% content_for(:title) { "Install Dotted with ONCE" } %>

<main data-page="once" data-size="md">
  <section class="once-card" aria-labelledby="once-heading">
    <h1 id="once-heading">Dotted <small>ONCE-ready</small></h1>
    <h2>Put it on your own server, without a subscription.</h2>
    <p>
      ONCE installs Docker apps with one command. It handles HTTPS, persistent
      storage, updates, and backups. You keep the machine and the data. Dotted
      is source-available under the <a href="https://osaasy.dev/">O’Saasy license</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      These steps use Dotted’s <a href="https://github.com/spacepolice10/digibujo#install-with-once">ONCE-ready Docker image</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section data-layout="column" aria-label="Install Dotted with ONCE">
    <article data-elevation="1">
      <header>
        <h2>What you need</h2>
        <p>A computer you control, a hostname, and an email service for sign-in codes.</p>
      </header>
      <main>
        <h3 id="once-host-heading">A host</h3>
        <section data-layout="grid" aria-labelledby="once-host-heading">
          <figure>
            <%= image_tag "landings/host.jpg", alt: "", width: 80, height: 80, loading: "lazy" %>
          </figure>
          <p>Use an ONCE-supported computer or VPS. Keep ports 80 and 443 available for web traffic.</p>
        </section>

        <h3 id="once-hostname-heading">A hostname</h3>
        <section data-layout="grid" aria-labelledby="once-hostname-heading">
          <figure>
            <%= image_tag "landings/hostname.jpg", alt: "", width: 80, height: 80, loading: "lazy" %>
          </figure>
          <p>Point a DNS A record, such as <code>dotted.example.com</code>, to the host’s public IP address.</p>
        </section>

        <h3 id="once-smtp-heading">SMTP credentials</h3>
        <section data-layout="grid" aria-labelledby="once-smtp-heading">
          <figure>
            <%= image_tag "landings/smtp.jpg", alt: "", width: 80, height: 80, loading: "lazy" %>
          </figure>
          <p>Dotted signs people in with emailed codes. Set up outgoing mail before anyone tries to sign in.</p>
        </section>
      </main>
    </article>

    <article data-elevation="1">
      <header>
        <h2>Installation</h2>
        <p>Install ONCE, point DNS, then deploy the Dotted image.</p>
      </header>
      <main>
        <h3>Install ONCE</h3>
        <p>Open the host’s terminal or connect with SSH, then run:</p>
        <pre><code>curl https://get.once.com | sh</code></pre>

        <h3>Point DNS</h3>
        <p>Create an A record for your chosen hostname. Set it to the host’s public IP address before deployment.</p>

        <h3>Deploy Dotted</h3>
        <pre><code>once deploy ghcr.io/spacepolice10/digibujo:latest --host dotted.example.com</code></pre>
        <p>Replace the example hostname with yours, then open it when ONCE reports that the app is running.</p>
      </main>
    </article>

    <article data-elevation="1">
      <header>
        <h2>After it boots</h2>
        <p>Configure email and keep the storage volume backed up.</p>
      </header>
      <main>
        <h3>Configure email</h3>
        <p>Use ONCE’s Email Settings for your SMTP server. Dotted reads the SMTP address, port, username, password, domain, and sender address from the environment. Set <code>APP_HOST</code> to your public hostname.</p>

        <h3>Sign in</h3>
        <p>Open your Dotted hostname and request a sign-in code. Delivery needs working SMTP settings.</p>
      </main>
    </article>

  </section>
</main>
